<article class="env-lemma" id="07S0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07S0">Lemma <span data-tag="07S0">37.45.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a separated, locally quasi-finite morphism with $Y$ affine. Then every finite set of points of $X$ is contained in an open affine of $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $x_1, \ldots , x_ n \in X$. Choose a quasi-compact open $U \subset X$ with $x_ i \in U$. Then $U \to Y$ is quasi-affine by Lemma <a href="/tag/02LR" data-tag="02LR">37.43.2</a>. Hence there exists an affine open $V \subset U$ containing $x_1, \ldots , x_ n$ by Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/01ZY" data-tag="01ZY">28.30.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>